# rollback-contact.api — public contract for glideclash
# This file is the authoritative specification. Implement it exactly.

## Package
Only package glideclash.api is part of the public surface of /app/lib/glideclash.jar.

## Enums
Action: NEUTRAL, NORTH, NORTHEAST, EAST, SOUTHEAST, SOUTH, SOUTHWEST, WEST, NORTHWEST
Axis: X, Y
Side: LEFT, RIGHT
InputStatus: STORED, REVISED, IDEMPOTENT, STALE_SEQUENCE, TOO_OLD, CONFLICT, UNKNOWN_PLAYER, INVALID_INPUT
EventKind: GOAL, WALL, GATE, BUMPER, PADDLE, PUCK

## Records
Rules(width, height, subframes, rollbackWindow, friction, maxSpeed, serveSpeed)
PuckSeed(id, x, y, vx, vy, radius)
PaddleSeed(id, player, x, y, radius, speed, homeMinX, homeMaxX, homeMinY, homeMaxY)
Bumper(id, x, y, radius, kick)
Gate(id, axis, coordinate, low, high, blockedSign)  # blockedSign is -1 or 1
Goal(id, side, low, high)
Blueprint(rules, pucks, paddles, bumpers, gates, goals)
InputFrame(player, tick, sequence, action)
InputReceipt(status, corrections)
ArenaEvent(tick, subframe, kind, primaryId, secondaryId)
BodyView(id, x, y, vx, vy, xRemainder, yRemainder)
PendingServe(puckId, exitedSide)
PlayerAction(player, action)
Snapshot(headTick, leftScore, rightScore, pucks, paddles, pendingServes, actions)
GlideFrame(tick, corrected, snapshot, events)

## Engine
static Engine start(Blueprint blueprint)
long headTick()
Snapshot snapshot()
InputReceipt submit(InputFrame input)
List<GlideFrame> advanceTo(long targetTick)
Engine fork()

## Exceptions
BlueprintException extends IllegalArgumentException with code() and id()
PhysicsException extends IllegalStateException with code(), tick(), subframe()
PhysicsException codes: arithmetic | impact-limit | ricochet-cap

## Null policy
No public method accepts or returns null.
Null top-level Engine argument -> NullPointerException before mutation.
Null Blueprint component, list, or list member -> BlueprintException code null-member id -
subject to validation precedence.

## Identifiers
Match [a-z][a-z0-9-]{0,23}. Compare by unsigned UTF-8 bytes (ASCII order).

## Blueprint validation
Order-independent; complete before Engine allocation.
Codes (precedence): rules, duplicate-id, player, bounds, home, goal, gate, overlap, null-member.
Lexically smallest offending id wins within a code.
Rules: width/height 100..1000000; subframes 2..256; rollbackWindow 1..256;
friction 0..maxSpeed; maxSpeed 1..100000 and <= min(width,height)/2; serveSpeed 1..maxSpeed.
Lists nonempty except bumpers and gates. Exactly one LEFT and one RIGHT goal.
Shared id namespace. Circles wholly inside rink. Home contains paddle circle.
No seed/bumper overlaps; no seed/gate intersection at tick zero.

## Timeline
State is at beginning of headTick (starts 0).
advanceTo(T): T in [headTick, Long.MAX_VALUE]; simulate headTick..T-1; return one GlideFrame each;
set headTick=T. Smaller T -> IllegalArgumentException. Same T -> empty immutable list.

## Inputs
One effective action per player per tick. Missing authority predicts prior effective action (start NEUTRAL).
Same player+tick: identical -> IDEMPOTENT; lower seq -> STALE_SEQUENCE; equal seq different action -> CONFLICT;
higher seq replaces. Invalid/stale/conflict/too-old leave state unchanged.
Future/current accepted -> STORED. Past accepted in window -> REVISED; else TOO_OLD.
REVISED restores beginning of tick, preserves later authority, resimulates to former head.
Corrections: only changed frames, corrected=true, sorted by tick.
A tick's paddle action is authoritative when an InputFrame for that player+tick is stored;
otherwise it is predicted. This distinction changes paddle impulse (below).

## Event field semantics (required)
ArenaEvent.primaryId / secondaryId by kind:
- GOAL: primaryId = puck id; secondaryId = goal id. Entering LEFT goal increments rightScore and
  queues PendingServe(puckId, LEFT). Entering RIGHT goal increments leftScore and queues
  PendingServe(puckId, RIGHT). No WALL event is emitted for that puck in the same subframe.
- WALL: primaryId = puck id; secondaryId is exactly one of: left | right | top | bottom
  (the side that was penetrated). Never "-" and never a goal id.
- GATE: primaryId = puck id; secondaryId = gate id.
- BUMPER: primaryId = puck id; secondaryId = bumper id.
- PADDLE: primaryId = puck id; secondaryId = paddle id.
- PUCK: primaryId = lexical-smaller puck id; secondaryId = lexical-larger puck id.

Events sort by subframe, kind (GOAL,WALL,GATE,BUMPER,PADDLE,PUCK), primaryId, secondaryId.

## Physics
Signed long with addExact/subtractExact/multiplyExact. Overflow or unresolved contact ->
PhysicsException arithmetic|impact-limit; transactional for the entire advanceTo call.
Tick start counters (reset every tick before subframes): bumperResponseOrdinal=0;
ricochetCount[puckId]=0 for all pucks.
Tick: respawn scored pucks; choose actions; subframes 0..subframes-1.
Paddle remainders zero each tick; puck remainders persist across ticks unless purged below.
Per axis: remainder+=velocity; delta=floorDiv(remainder,subframes); remainder=floorMod; pos+=delta.
Paddles move then clamp to radius-shrunk home (zero clamped-axis remainder); then pucks;
then boundaries; then contacts.

### Boundaries (per puck, per subframe)
1) Goal test before walls. Goal uses puck center y in [goal.low, goal.high] and radius crossing
   the LEFT (x-radius<0) or RIGHT (x+radius>width) mouth. On goal: emit GOAL, score, deactivate puck,
   queue serve; skip walls/gates for that puck this subframe.
2) Walls: if x-radius<0 -> clamp x=radius, if vx<0 then vx=-vx, purge xRemainder=0, emit WALL secondaryId=left.
   Else if x+radius>width -> clamp x=width-radius, if vx>0 then vx=-vx, purge xRemainder=0, emit WALL right.
   Then independently: y-radius<0 -> top; y+radius>height -> bottom (same reflect+purge on that axis).
   Horizontal walls are resolved before vertical walls. Multiple WALL events in one subframe are allowed.
3) Gates: one-way by blockedSign on prior->current crossing of coordinate within [low,high] expanded by radius.
   On block: place puck just outside on the blocked side, negate the gate-axis velocity, purge the gate-axis
   remainder, emit GATE. After a GATE reflection, immediately re-run step (2) walls for that puck only.

### Serve / respawn
Pending serves apply at the beginning of the next tick, before actions, sorted by puckId ascending.
Respawn at (width/2, height/2) with remainders 0, vy=0, active=true.
Serve direction is AWAY from the exited mouth:
  exitedSide LEFT  -> vx = +serveSpeed
  exitedSide RIGHT -> vx = -serveSpeed
(The scorer is the opposite side; the puck is served back toward the scorer's half.)

### Contacts
Contact axis: X if |dx|>=|dy| else Y; equal centers force X oriented with lexical-smaller id on the negative side.
Separation always when overlapping; velocity response only when approaching on the contact axis.
Islands: connected components via puck-puck overlap; attach bumper/paddle contacts; order components by
least puck id; within a component sort contacts by kind rank BUMPER,PADDLE,PUCK then primaryId then secondaryId.
Up to 4 sweeps per subframe; rediscover islands each sweep; impact-limit if approaching overlap remains.
PUCK velocity response: swap contact-axis velocity components only.
BUMPER velocity response (after separate):
  outwardSign = sign of (puckCenter - bumperCenter) on contact axis; if zero, use contact orientation (+1/-1).
  bumperResponseOrdinal += 1  (tick-global, across subframes)
  effectiveKick = floorDiv(bumper.kick, bumperResponseOrdinal)
  v_axis = clampSpeed( -(v_axis) + outwardSign * effectiveKick , maxSpeed )
  Emit BUMPER only when a velocity response runs (once per puck|bumper pair per subframe).
PADDLE velocity response (after separate), contact axis only:
  if the paddle owner's action for this tick is authoritative:
    v_axis = clampSpeed( 2 * paddle_v_axis - puck_v_axis , maxSpeed )
  else (predicted action):
    v_axis = clampSpeed( paddle_v_axis - puck_v_axis , maxSpeed )
  Orthogonal puck component unchanged. Emit PADDLE when velocity response runs.
Separation split for two pucks: let lo=lexical-smaller id, hi=larger; gap = radiiSum - |centerDelta|.
lo moves floor((gap+1)/2) and hi moves floor(gap/2), each away from the other along the axis
(if centers equal, lo moves negative, hi positive).

### Ricochet cap
Each emitted WALL, GATE, BUMPER, or PADDLE event increments ricochetCount[primaryId]
(PUCK events do not count). If any puck's count exceeds floorDiv(subframes, 2) during the tick,
throw PhysicsException code ricochet-cap at that tick/subframe and roll back the entire advanceTo.

End-of-tick friction on pucks (each component moves toward 0 by at most friction, never crosses 0);
paddles velocity zero (remainders published then reset next tick).

## Snapshots
Structural record equality. fork deep-copies. Defensive immutable collections.
